# SPRINT MEM — unbounded-growth stops (caps)

**Marker:** `SPRINT_MEM_CAPS_2026-08-13`
**Date:** 2026-08-13
**Role:** MEM. Read-only except this file.
**Method:** file read + ripgrep. No `oodac check oodac/main.oo`. No new clock.
**Pin used (not re-timed):** SPRINT live 28 s / 12 GB RSS after B8.

## Verdict

1048576 is **not** one dual cap. It is a **char** cap in lex/check and a **token-row** cap in collect/tokenize. Live scanners always move `i` on continue, so tokenize does **not** spin under the token cap today. There is **no** `i`-progress assert; a SKIP that returned the same `i` would loop forever without hitting 1048576. F26 8 GiB WARN / 32 GiB FAIL are live consts, not comments. B8 binds are `List[String]` + `list_push`. Residual: **12 GB still > 8 GiB WARN**.

## Bound table

| Site | What 1048576 counts | Compare | On trip | Both? |
|------|---------------------|---------|---------|-------|
| `ooda/oodac/token_stream.oo:22` `collect_tokens` | **token rows** (`list_len(out)`) | `>=` | `ERR lex too many tokens` + `process_exit(1)` | no |
| `ooda/oodac/token_fmt.oo:26` `tokenize_lines` | **token rows** (`list_len(toks)`) | `>` | same ERR + exit | no |
| `ooda/oodac/lex.oo:16` `lex_all` | **chars** (`chars_len(src)`) | `>` | `Err("source exceeds 1MiB limit")` | no |
| `ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo:30` `run_check_core_binds` | **chars** expanded src | `>` | `ERR check source exceeds 1MiB expanded limit` + exit | no |
| `ooda/oodac/check_mod.oo:16` `run_check_module_body` | **chars** module body | `>` | same check ERR + exit | no |

No site caps tokens **and** chars. Together: lex/check stop a source longer than 1 MiB chars; collect stops a list of 1048576 tok_line rows.

`tokenize_lines` runs `lex_all` first, then `collect_tokens`, then `list_len > 1048576`. Collect already `process_exit`s at `>= 1048576`, so the tokenize post-cap is **dead**. A 1 MiB file of one-char punct (`n == 1048576`, lex allows `>`) can fill 1048576 rows and hit collect before EOF. Complementary, not redundant.

Related (not 1048576): `cli_parse.oo:67` root `file_size > 65536` (64 KiB). Comment on check_drive still says per-file 64 KiB at load; that gate is the root CLI path, not every import.

## Tokenize loop — does `i` always increase?

`tokenize_lines` does not walk. The walker is `collect_tokens` (`token_stream.oo:21-54`).

```
i = 0
while cont:
  if list_len(out) >= 1048576: exit
  if i >= n: push EOF; stop
  p = lex_step(src, i, line, col)
  ERR  -> stop (no i write)
  SKIP -> i = parse_int(p[1])   // no list_push
  TOK  -> i = parse_int(p[1]); push row; EOF -> stop
```

`i` is **not** `i = i + 1`. Progress is whatever `lex_step` packs.

Live scanners (read):

| Pack | File | Next `i` vs `i0` |
|------|------|------------------|
| SKIP space/tab/nl | `token_scan_ws.oo:52-61` | `i0 + 1` |
| SKIP `//` | `token_scan_ws.oo:63-82` | at least `i0 + 2` |
| TOK string/num/ident/punct | `token_scan_*.oo` | at least `i0 + 1` |
| miss | `token_next.oo:40` `pack_err` | collect stops |

`parse_int` (`tc_parse_int.oo`) folds digit text; `i.to_string()` from those packs is a non-neg Int. Not a reset.

**Non-advance under the cap?** Not with these scanners. **Structural hole:** the 1048576 cap is on **rows**, not iterations. SKIP does not grow `out`. A SKIP (or a `parse_int` that returned `<= i`) would spin **forever below the cap**. Collect has no `if i <= prev { ERR }`. Check walk in `check_drive.oo:49-72` **does** have that (iter + `pos == prev_pos`). That guard is not on tokenize.

`lex.oo:22` `while i < n` (n already `<= 1048576`): every arm does `i = i + k` (`k >= 1`) or returns Err. `lex_scan_*` start at `pos + 1`. Inner `//` stop on `\n` without eating it, but `i` already moved by 2. **lex `i` always increases.**

Time below the cap is still Θ(n²) `char_at` (prior r2_memory). That is CPU, not an infinite loop and not unbounded heap. Heap of the token list is O(rows) up to 1048576 TSV strings.

## F26 — 8 GiB WARN / 32 GiB FAIL is code

Not a comment-only claim.

`ooda/scripts/harness_f26_residual_smoke.oo`:

- L17 `WARN_RSS_KB = 8 * 1024 * 1024`  → 8_388_608 KB = **8 GiB**
- L18 `FAIL_RSS_KB = 32 * 1024 * 1024` → 33_554_432 KB = **32 GiB**
- L17 `TIMEOUT_S = 180`
- L43 `expect_lt(rss, FAIL_RSS_KB)` live fail-closed
- L44 `if rss > WARN_RSS_KB { println("WARN … > 8 GiB") }` live

`ooda/scripts/harness_f26_residual_smoke.sh`:

- L11–12 same arithmetic
- L50–51 live `rss -gt FAIL` / `rss -gt WARN`

GNU `/usr/bin/time -v` “Maximum resident set size” is kbytes. The multiply is in KB. Honest.

Harness does **not** pin 28 s or 12 GB. Those are the SPRINT B8 board, not the gate. `.sh` L2 header still says “32s, 22.8 GB” (old ELF). Stale comment; live numbers are 180 s / 8 / 32 GiB.

12 GB vs gates (no new RSS this turn):

- 12 GiB = 12_582_912 KB **>** 8_388_608 KB WARN
- 12 GB decimal ≈ 11_718_750 KB still **>** WARN
- both **<** 33_554_432 KB FAIL

## B8 binds — List[String], not concat

`tc_names.oo:27` `let mut binds: List[String] = list_new();`

Spot-check one append (`tc_names.oo:55`, fn-name pre-bind):

`binds = list_push(binds, fname + "@0");`

Not `binds = binds + …`. Ripgrep `binds = binds +` in `tc_names.oo` + `tc_scope.oo` = **0**. Seven bind sites + two extra_binds-split pushes are `list_push`. `scope_has` / `drop_depth` take `List[String]`. `name + "@" + ds` is the small payload string, not the old whole-table concat.

Leftover **outside** B8 files: `check_scan.oo:178,187` `binds = binds + cur + "@0\t"` and `check_mod.oo:64` `names = names + scan_fn_names(...)`. That is the extra_binds **String** builder for np>12, not the typecheck accumulator.

## Residual

| Item | Sev | Note |
|------|-----|------|
| **12 GB still > 8 GiB WARN** | MED | B8 pin. Under 32 GiB FAIL. Not 1–2 s / 39 MB. |
| Token cap ≠ iter cap | LOW | SKIP non-advance would ignore 1048576. Live scanners do not. No `i` guard. |
| `tokenize_lines` row cap dead | LOW | Collect already exits at `>=`. |
| Char cap after expand | MED (old) | 1 MiB fires after concat; root 64 KiB only on CLI entry. |
| `char_at` Θ(n²) below 1 MiB | MED (old) | Time, not unbounded rows. |
| extra_binds still String concat | LOW | `check_scan` / `check_mod` names builder. |
| 28 s / 12 GB | — | Board pin. This turn did not re-run check. |

**MEM return:** bound table above. Residual: **12 GB still > 8 GiB WARN**.

end of sprint_mem_caps.oot
